WEBVTT

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:07.997
Your agent just got a workplace.

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:10.056
A chat that streams.

00:00:10.856 --> 00:00:12.285
A memory that is yours.

00:00:13.085 --> 00:00:15.346
Routines, a vault, and an admin room.

00:00:16.146 --> 00:00:17.661
All built from one folder.

00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:23.241
Ask a question and the answer streams in as it is written.

00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:27.006
When the agent reaches for a tool, you see a card for it.

00:00:27.806 --> 00:00:30.899
And when an action needs your say so, it stops and asks.

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:33.491
You approve, and it carries on.

00:00:35.891 --> 00:00:37.043
Need a specialist?

00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:40.744
Pick a sub-agent in the header and talk to it directly.

00:00:41.544 --> 00:00:43.102
The researcher looks things up.

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:45.480
The writer drafts replies.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.414
Each one keeps its own conversations.

00:00:52.011 --> 00:00:53.696
Every conversation is kept.

00:00:54.496 --> 00:00:55.712
Search by title.

00:00:56.512 --> 00:00:58.283
Filter by agent or source.

00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:01.430
Page through them, and act on many at once.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.155
Routines are agent work on a schedule.

00:01:06.955 --> 00:01:11.371
Ask once, and it runs every weekday morning and leaves a report each time.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:13.430
Members see their own.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.617
Admins see everyone's.

00:01:17.316 --> 00:01:19.727
The registry shows what the agent can use.

00:01:20.047 --> 00:01:21.839
Tools, grouped by what they do.

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:23.823
Skills you can open and read.

00:01:24.143 --> 00:01:25.636
And the folders it may touch.

00:01:26.637 --> 00:01:28.066
Memory comes in layers.

00:01:28.386 --> 00:01:30.584
Notes about you, which are yours alone.

00:01:30.904 --> 00:01:33.186
Notes the agent shares across its team.

00:01:33.506 --> 00:01:37.090
And the memory of each conversation, which you can clear any time.

00:01:38.089 --> 00:01:39.518
Secrets go in the vault.

00:01:39.838 --> 00:01:45.492
The value is sealed and never shown again, and each one says what it is for and which hosts may see it.

00:01:46.491 --> 00:01:48.603
Admins see the agent as it really is.

00:01:48.923 --> 00:01:55.195
The composition draws itself live: what reaches it, its sub-agents, its tools, and where it reaches out.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.798
Browse its files, and watch its usage.

00:01:58.798 --> 00:02:01.891
Gateways put the agent on Telegram, Slack and more.

00:02:02.211 --> 00:02:05.710
Each one shows its state and its chats, and a click reconnects it.

00:02:06.711 --> 00:02:10.060
Logs by area: the agent, the routines, the heartbeat.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.666
Search them, filter by level, and let them refresh live.

00:02:13.986 --> 00:02:15.458
Secrets are never written.

00:02:16.457 --> 00:02:17.673
Access is simple.

00:02:17.993 --> 00:02:20.446
Issue a named token, and it is shown once.

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:23.476
See who can sign in, and choose who is an admin.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.184
Data and backups.

00:02:26.504 --> 00:02:28.979
See where everything lives and how big it is.

00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:32.755
Make a backup in one click, and restore one just as easily.

00:02:33.755 --> 00:02:35.206
And it is yours to shape.

00:02:35.526 --> 00:02:36.614
Light or dark.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.128
Your accent colour.

00:02:38.448 --> 00:02:40.923
Text size, and how dense the page feels.

00:02:41.243 --> 00:02:42.907
The page remembers your choice.

00:02:43.907 --> 00:02:45.976
On a phone the menu becomes a drawer.

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:51.352
Targets are big, focus is always visible, and the whole page works from the keyboard.

00:02:52.352 --> 00:02:56.213
Everything you just saw is also in the terminal, and in the API.

00:02:56.533 --> 00:03:03.168
The same notes, routines and conversations, from a bxAgents command or a plain HTTP call.

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.020
BxAgents.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.497
One folder, one command, a whole agent workplace.

00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:13.551
Run bxAgents new, and read the docs on the project page.

00:03:13.871 --> 00:03:15.300
Your agent is waiting.

